   9| - **Safety First**: Destructive operations require explicit vitals
  10| 
  11| ### 1.2 Design Goals
   8| - **Minimal Overhead**: Clear structure without unnecessary boilerplate
   9| - **Intuitive Symbols**: Natural symbols (`>>`, `::`, `@`, `!`) map to actions
  10| - **Error Resilience**: Clear error patterns for common mistakes
  11| - **Extensible**: Easy to add new operations while maintaining consistency
  12| 
  13| ## 2. Core Symbols
  14| 
  15| | Symbol | Name | Purpose |
  16| |--------|------|---------|
  17| | `>>` | Thought | Reasoning, context, intent |
  18| | `::` | Action | Tool calls, operations |
  19| | `@` | Target | File paths, identifiers |
  20| | `!` | Alert | Critical warnings |
  21| | `<<<` / `>>>` | Content | Data blocks, file contents |
  22| 
  23| ## 3. Vitals System
  24| 
  25| ### 3.1 Vitals Format
  26| ```
  27| ::c[0-1] ::s[0-1] ::m[0-1] ::f[0-1]
  28| ```
  29| 
  30| | Vital | Full Name | Description |
  31| |-------|-----------|-------------|
  32| | `::c` | Confidence | 確信度 (0-1) |
  33| | `::s` | Safety | 安全性 (0-1), <0.5 requires confirmation |
  34| | `::m` | Memory | メモリ負荷 (0-1) |
  35| | `::f` | Focus | フォーカス (0-1) |
  36| 
  37| ### 3.2 Vitals Thresholds
  38| - **::s < 0.5**: System pauses for user confirmation
  39| - **::c < 0.7**: Recommend investigation mode
  40| - **::f < 0.5**: Suggest context refresh
  41| 
  42| ## 4. Action Types
  43| 
  44| ### 4.1 Single Action
  45| ```sym-ops
  46| >> Reasoning about the action
  47| 
  48| ::c0.9 ::s1.0 ::m0.1 ::f0.95
  49| 
  49| ::action_name @path
  50| <<<
  51| content here
  52| >>>
  53| ```
  54| 
  55| ### 4.2 Batch Execution
  56| ```sym-ops
  57| >> Multiple independent operations
  58| 
  59| ::c0.9 ::s1.0 ::m0.2 ::f1.0
  60| 
  61| ::execute_batch
  62| <<<
  63| action1 @path1
  64| content1
  65| %%%
  66| action2 @path2
  67| content2
  68| >>>
  69| ```
  69| 
  70| ## 5. Tool Reference
  71| 
  72| ### 5.1 File Operations
  73| 
  74| #### read_file
  74| ```sym-ops
  75| ::read_file @path
  76| ```
  76| - **Parameters**: None required
  77| - **Returns**: File content with line numbers
  78| 
  79| #### write_file
  79| ```sym-ops
  80| ::write_file @path
  81| <<<
  82| file content
  83| >>>
  84| ```
  84| - **Parameters**: None
  85| - **Returns**: Confirmation message
  86| 
  87| #### create_file
  87| ```sym-ops
  88| ::create_file @path
  89| <<<
  86| content
  87| >>>
  88| ```
  88| - Same as write_file
  89| 
  90| #### delete_file
  90| ```sym-Ops
  91| ::delete_file @path
  92| ```
  92| - **Safety**: Requires ::s < 0.5
  93| 
  93| ### 5.2 Line-Based Editing
  94| 
  94| #### edit_lines
  94| ```sym-ops
  95| ::edit_lines @path
  96| start=1
  97| end=5
  98| <<<
  99| new content
  100| >>>
  101| ```
  101| - **Parameters**:
  102|   - `start`: Starting line number (1-indexed)
  103|   - `end`: Ending line number (inclusive)
  104|   - `content`: New content to replace lines
  105| - **Returns**: Before/after preview
  106| 
  107| #### replace_in_file
  107| ```sym-ops
  108| ::replace_in_file @path
  109| search="old text"
  110| replace="new text"
  111| ```
  111| - **Parameters**:
  112|   - `search`: Text to find
  113|   - `replace`: Replacement text
  114| 
  115| ### 5.3 Directory Operations
  115| 
  116| #### list_directory
  116| ```sym-ops
  117| ::list_directory @path
  118| ```
  118| - **Parameters**: Optional path
  119| - **Returns**: List of files/dirs
  120| 
  121| #### get_project_tree
  121| ```sym-ops
  122| ::get_project_tree @path depth=3
  123| ```
  123| - **Parameters**:
  124|   - `depth`: Maximum depth to traverse
  125| 
  126| ### 5.4 Search Operations
  126| 
  127| #### find_files
  127| ```sym-ops
  128| ::find_files pattern="*.py"
  129| ```
  129| - **Parameters**:
  130|   - `pattern`: Glob pattern
  131| 
  132| ### 5.5 Planning
  132| 
  133| #### propose_plan
  133| ```sym-ops
  134| ::propose_plan
  134| <<<
  135| ## ステップ1
  136| Description
  137| ## ステップ2
  138| Description
  139| >>>
  140| ```
  140| 
  141| ### 5.6 Terminal Actions
  141| 
  142| #### note
  142| ```sym-ops
  143| ::note
  144| <<<
  145| message
  146| >>>
  147| ```
  147| 
  148| #### response
  148| ```sym-ops
  149| ::response
  150| <<<
  151| Short response (max 3-4 sentences)
  152| >>>
  153| ```
  153| 
  154| #### report
  154| ```sym-ops
  155| ::report
  155| <<<
  156| ## 要約
  157| Brief summary
  158| 
  159| ## 詳細
  159| Detailed analysis
  160| 
  161| ## 結論
  161| Conclusion
  162| >>>
  163| ```
  163| 
  164| #### finish
  164| ```sym-ops
  165| ::finish
  165| <<<
  166| Task completed successfully
  167| >>>
  168| ```
  168| 
  169| #### exit
  169| ```sym-ops
  170| ::exit
  171| ```
  171| 
  172| ### 5.7 Investigation Mode
  172| 
  173| #### investigate
  173| ```sym-ops
  174| ::investigate
  174| <<<
  175| Reason for investigation
  176| >>>
  177| ```
  177| 
  178| #### submit_hypothesis
  178| ```sym-ops
  179| ::submit_hypothesis
  179| <<<
  180| Description of what to test
  181| >>>
  182| ```
  182| 
  183| #### finish_investigation
  183| ```sym-ops
  183| ::finish_investigation
  184| <<<
  185| Conclusion and findings
  186| >>>
  187| ```
  187| 
  188| ### 5.8 Analysis Tools
  188| 
  189| #### analyze_structure
  189| ```sym-ops
  190| ::analyze_structure @path
  191| ```
  191| 
  192| #### generate_code
  192| ```sym-ops
  193| ::generate_code @path
  193| <<<
  194| Specifications for code generation
  195| >>>
  196| ```
  196| 
  197| ### 5.9 Command Execution
  197| 
  198| #### run_command
  198| ```sym-ops
  199| ::run_command
  199| <<<
  200| command to execute
  201| >>>
  202| ```
  202| - **Safety**: Requires user approval before execution
  203| 
  203| ## 6. Content Blocks
  204| 
  204| ### 6.1 Block Delimiters
  205| - **Opening**: `<<<` at column 0
  206| - **Closing**: `>>>` at column 0
  207| - **Content**: Raw text, no markdown formatting inside
  208| 
  209| ### 6.2 Block Types
  209| | Type | Usage |
  210| |------|-------|
  211| | File content | write_file, create_file, edit_lines |
  212| | Message | note, response, report |
  212| | Plan | propose_plan |
  213| | Command | run_command |
  213| 
  214| ## 7. Error Handling
  214| 
  215| ### 7.1 Common Errors
  215| | Error | Cause | Fix |
  216| |-------|-------|-----|
  217| | `Missing vitals` | No ::c ::s ::m ::f line | Add vitals before action |
  218| | `Invalid symbol` | Unknown action name | Check spelling |
  219| | `Missing target` | No @path for file operations | Add @path |
  220| | `Block not closed` | Missing >>> | Close all content blocks |
  221| 
  222| ### 7.2 Recovery Patterns
  222| - **Parse error**: Retry with corrected syntax
  223| - **Tool failure**: Enter investigate mode
  224| - **Missing context**: Use recall or read_file
  225| 
  225| ## 8. Examples
  226| 
  226| ### 8.1 Complete Workflow
  226| ```sym-ops
  227| >> Need to analyze a file
  228| 
  229| ::c0.9 ::s1.0 ::m0.1 ::f0.95
  229| 
  230| ::read_file @src/main.py
  231| 
  232| >> Found the issue. Now I'll fix it.
  233| 
  234| ::c0.95 ::s0.8 ::m0.2 ::f1.0
  234| 
  235| ::edit_lines @src/main.py
  235| start=10
  236| end=15
  237| <<<
  238| # Fixed version
  239| def new_function():
  240|     return True
  241| >>>
  242| ```
  242| 
  243| ## 9. Version History
  243| 
  243| ### v3.1 (Current)
  243| - Added batch execution support
  244| - Improved error messages
  245| - Standardized vitals format
  246| 
  246| ### v3.0
  246| - Initial stable release
  246| - Core symbol system
  246| - Vitals framework
  246| 
  246| ---
  246| 
  246| *Last updated: 2024*
